  "hints": [
    "Write down the state needed between ticks: the buffer contents, each producer's position in its item list, and when each participant may next try.",
    "Simulate one tick at a time exactly as specified: the produce phase in index order, then the consume phase in index order, using a FIFO queue for the buffer.",
    "To avoid stepping through long idle stretches, notice that a tick where nobody acts leaves the state unchanged except the clock. Jump directly to the smallest next-try tick that is still in the future (among producers with items left and all consumers)."
  ],
  "solution": {
    "js": "function bufferTrace(capacity, producers, consumers) {\n  const buffer = []\n  let head = 0\n  const pNext = producers.map(() => 1)\n  const pPos = producers.map(() => 0)\n  const cNext = consumers.map(() => 1)\n  let remaining = producers.reduce((sum, [, items]) => sum + items.length, 0)\n  const trace = []\n  let tick = 1\n  while (remaining > 0) {\n    let acted = false\n    producers.forEach(([gap, items], i) => {\n      if (pPos[i] < items.length && pNext[i] <= tick && buffer.length - head < capacity) {\n        buffer.push(items[pPos[i]++])\n        pNext[i] = tick + gap\n        acted = true\n      }\n    })\n    consumers.forEach((gap, j) => {\n      if (cNext[j] <= tick && head < buffer.length) {\n        trace.push([tick, j, buffer[head++]])\n        cNext[j] = tick + gap\n        remaining--\n        acted = true\n      }\n    })\n    if (acted) {\n      tick++\n      continue\n    }\n    let next = Infinity\n    producers.forEach(([, items], i) => {\n      if (pPos[i] < items.length && pNext[i] > tick) next = Math.min(next, pNext[i])\n    })\n    for (const t of cNext) if (t > tick) next = Math.min(next, t)\n    tick = next\n  }\n  return trace\n}\n",
    "py": "from collections import deque\n\n\ndef buffer_trace(capacity, producers, consumers):\n    buffer = deque()\n    p_next = [1] * len(producers)\n    p_pos = [0] * len(producers)\n    c_next = [1] * len(consumers)\n    remaining = sum(len(items) for _, items in producers)\n    trace = []\n    tick = 1\n    while remaining:\n        acted = False\n        for i, (gap, items) in enumerate(producers):\n            if p_pos[i] < len(items) and p_next[i] <= tick and len(buffer) < capacity:\n                buffer.append(items[p_pos[i]])\n                p_pos[i] += 1\n                p_next[i] = tick + gap\n                acted = True\n        for j, gap in enumerate(consumers):\n            if c_next[j] <= tick and buffer:\n                trace.append([tick, j, buffer.popleft()])\n                c_next[j] = tick + gap\n                remaining -= 1\n                acted = True\n        if acted:\n            tick += 1\n            continue\n        waiting = [p_next[i] for i, (_, items) in enumerate(producers) if p_pos[i] < len(items) and p_next[i] > tick]\n        waiting += [t for t in c_next if t > tick]\n        tick = min(waiting)\n    return trace\n",
    "explanation": "The solution follows the rules literally: each tick runs the produce phase then the consume phase in index order, keeping a FIFO buffer and a next-try tick for every participant. If a tick does nothing, every participant that may try is blocked and nothing changes until some cooldown ends, so the clock jumps straight to the earliest future next-try tick. That bounds the number of simulated ticks by about twice the number of actions."
  },
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(N * (P + C))",
    "space": "O(N + P + C)",
    "notes": "N items, P producers, C consumers. Each tick that acts performs at least one of the 2N actions, and each idle tick is followed by a jump to a cooldown that some earlier action started, so at most O(N) ticks are simulated, each scanning everyone once. Heaps of ready times can cut the per-tick scan further."
  },
  "followUps": [
    "Give consumers priorities so that, when several may take an item, the highest priority goes first. What changes?",
    "Return the maximum number of items that were ever in the buffer at once, and the total ticks producers spent blocked."
  ]
}
